sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor PAT as Patient
    participant PBX as Practice phone system (platform unconfirmed)
    participant HP as Hello Patient (PoC, US AWS)
    participant PCW as patientcomms.co.uk
    participant PC as PatientComms V3 (Dataphiles)
    participant MC as MyCare adaptor
    participant R4 as R4 practice database
    participant DW as Replication, DW and EDW

    rect rgb(219,234,254)
        Note over PAT,HP: 1 — The call, and where it lands
        PAT->>PBX: Rings the practice
        PBX->>PBX: Unanswered after ~5 rings, or out of hours
        PBX->>HP: Diverts to the practice's unique number
        HP-->>PAT: Identifies itself as an AI agent
    end

    rect rgb(220,252,231)
        Note over PAT,HP: 2 — Handled with no system access
        PAT->>HP: Asks to book an appointment
        Note over HP: No diary read. No diary write.<br/>No patient data held.
        HP-->>PAT: Texts or WhatsApps a booking link
    end

    rect rgb(254,243,199)
        Note over PAT,R4: 3 — The booking lands asynchronously
        PAT->>PCW: Opens the link and chooses a slot
        PCW->>PC: Submits the booking
        PC->>MC: Hands the write to the adaptor
        MC->>R4: Commits the appointment
        Note over MC,R4: Stated as within a maximum of 15 minutes.<br/>Sync interval or customer SLA — unconfirmed.
    end

    rect rgb(237,233,254)
        Note over R4,DW: 4 — The record becomes visible to the business
        R4->>DW: Replicates every 15 minutes
        DW->>DW: DW then EDW build, 10+ hours
        Note over DW: Not available until around<br/>mid-day the following day.
    end
